o make it compatible with `python -m unittest` or even better just make it unittest runnable that would be good. not sure why on earth I made this one example depend on pytest.   very strange\r\n\r\nnext, the way that `map_imperatively()` works now is not a direct port of `mapper()`, so the particular hook that's being used here, `__mapper_cls__`, which fortunately seems to be undocumented, has to actually return the `Mapper` class, not the `mapper` function's equivalent anymore.\r\n\r\nso it all works with this patch:\r\n\r\n```diff\r\ndiff --git a/examples/versioned_history/history_meta.py b/examples/versioned_history/history_meta.py\r\nindex 23bdc1e6f8..197fb68399 100644\r\n--- a/examples/versioned_history/history_meta.py\r\n+++ b/examples/versioned_history/history_meta.py\r\n@@ -11,7 +11,6 @@ from sqlalchemy import Table\r\n from sqlalchemy import util\r\n from sqlalchemy.ext.declarative import declared_attr\r\n from sqlalchemy.orm import attributes\r\n-from sqlalchemy.orm import mapper\r\n from sqlalchemy.orm import object_mapper\r\n from sqlalchemy.orm.exc import UnmappedColumnError\r\n from sqlalchemy.orm.relationships import RelationshipProperty\r\n@@ -151,7 +150,7 @@ def _history_mapper(local_mapper):\r\n         bases = local_mapper.base_mapper.class_.__bases__\r\n     versioned_cls = type.__new__(type, \"%sHistory\" % cls.__name__, bases, {})\r\n \r\n-    m = mapper(\r\n+    m = local_mapper.registry.map_imperatively(\r\n         versioned_cls,\r\n         table,\r\n         inherits=super_history_mapper,\r\n@@ -172,6 +171,7 @@ def _history_mapper(local_mapper):\r\n         if cls.use_mapper_versioning:\r\n             local_mapper.version_id_col = local_mapper.local_table.c.version\r\n \r\n+from sqlalchemy.orm import Mapper\r\n \r\n class Versioned:\r\n     use_mapper_versioning = False\r\n@@ -180,7 +180,7 @@ class Versioned:\r\n     @declared_attr\r\n     def __mapper_cls__(cls):\r\n         def map_(cls, *arg, **kw):\r\n-            mp = mapper(cls, *arg, **kw)\r\n+            mp = Mapper(cls, *arg, **kw)\r\n             _history_mapper(mp)\r\n             return mp\r\n \r\n```\r\n\r\nhowever that fix sucks.   I am not able to get a better fix working right now as the history thing seems to work in an extremely specific way.  so far it's looking like I have to add a new mapper configuration hook, this will require some effort.\r\n\r\n\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/comments/1413898779/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"id":8422310599,"node_id":"LE_lADOCX5JB85daoOezwAAAAH2AkLH","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/events/8422310599","actor":{"login":"zzzeek","id":128223,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyODIyMw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/128223?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zzzeek","html_url":"https://github.com/zzzeek","followers_url":"http